# What boot starts on the Raspberry Pi 5 once the drivers are running: a
# shell on the debug UART, the first, which boot waits for, so that its
# exit stops the system; font, the font service, which gives every
# program with a window its text's glyphs and starts before wm, which
# asks it first; and wm, which waits for the display hvs serves. No app
# is started here, so the desktop starts empty, and an app is started
# from the launcher. agentd, the agent's server, last: with no
# /etc/agent/config it says so and exits (make agent-etc makes one),
# and otherwise waits for its home's volume, the card's data
# partition, /Volumes/data, and serves agent, which run agent talks to.
# speech after it: with no /Volumes/data/speech/whistle.cact, which the
# installer fetches, it says so and exits; otherwise it reads Whistle,
# 14.6 s, and says what the microphone hears while F12 is held to the
# agent.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/font
start /sbin/wm
start /sbin/agentd
start /sbin/speech
